{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdtN3XLmhvyWacQ2hmRR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted an equal-weight portfolio of all 141 long-horizon industry trend signals: the `ma_50_200`, `tsmom_126` and `tsmom_252` signals for each of the 47 industries. It had a training Sharpe of 0.06 and failed the sealed 2000–2012 validation test, so I don't expect it to have real alpha.\n\nI made one backtest call and then submitted, rather than using the call budget for a search. When I split the training data, how well a signal did in 1970–1989 slightly predicted the reverse in 1990–1999 (correlation of Sharpe ratios −0.14). No family of signals made money consistently across the three decades. With no real edge to find, searching against the validation verdict would mostly turn up a lucky pass. I picked this portfolio because industry momentum has a known economic basis and the long-horizon trend families were the only ones that improved in the 1990s."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":9023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":568},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cf5ca9a7-3c26-48be-9091-fb6d1ced7c07","uuid":"54e9414f-2095-4893-8450-82ce7e71283b","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:30:26.493Z","request_id":"req_011CfdtN3DVByMwERt1cHxab"}
